You are localising a Korean webtoon into English for English-speaking readers.

{context}Korean: {text}
{type}{guide}
Write natural, idiomatic English that an English webtoon reader would expect, keeping the meaning, the intent and the intensity of the line; do not translate word for word. Start every sentence with a capital letter and use normal English capitalisation. Carry over the line's !, ? and ... where English uses them the same way, and add no stutters, ellipses, capitals or exclamation marks that the line does not call for. Romanise personal names; translate the meaning of skill, item, title and place names.

Give only the translation, after 'TRANSLATED_TEXT:'.
